# @zephyra/convex — local env for the Convex CLI.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The Convex CLI resolves both the functions directory
# (./convex) and its credentials relative to the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY. The
# backend lives here, so `convex dev` / `convex codegen` must be run from this
# package — and they read CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT from THIS directory's .env.local.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the deployment identity, because it is the
# file `npx convex dev` itself writes on first run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DRIFT HAZARD (V18) AND HOW IT IS HANDLED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next.js does not read a monorepo-root env file, so each app reads
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL from its OWN .env.local. The identity is therefore
# duplicated across FOUR gitignored files — not two, as this file said while
# apps/legacy still existed:
#
#   packages/convex/.env.local   CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT + the URLs  <- source of truth
#   apps/academia/.env.local     NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL,
#                                CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT
#   apps/backoffice/.env.local   NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL
#   apps/www/.env.local          NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL
#
# If they drift, an app talks to one backend while functions are pushed to
# another. NOTHING ERRORS. Queries return data from the wrong deployment, or
# return nothing and look like a seeding bug. Because .env.local is gitignored,
# no reviewer can ever catch it — so the guard is executable, not editorial:
#
#     pnpm convex:check    verify all four agree; exits 1 with a diff if not
#     pnpm convex:sync     propagate from this file into the apps, preserving
#                          every other key (secrets, comments, ordering)
#
# Both are safe to run repeatedly and skip any .env.local that does not exist, so
# a fresh clone and CI are no-ops. See ops/convex-identity.mjs.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SETUP, FROM A FRESH CLONE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   1. pnpm install
#   2. cd packages/convex && npx convex dev        # writes .env.local here
#   3. for each app: cp apps/<app>/.env.local.example apps/<app>/.env.local
#      then fill the per-app secrets that example documents. The exclusions in
#      those files are as load-bearing as the inclusions — apps/backoffice must
#      NOT gain LEARNER_JWT_SECRET, apps/academia must NOT gain SESSION_SECRET.
#   4. pnpm convex:sync                            # from the repo root
#   5. pnpm convex:check                           # must print OK
#
# Step 4 replaces the hand-copying that caused the drift. Re-run
# `pnpm convex:check` after any `npx convex dev` that switches deployment.
#
# NOTE: none of this touches the Convex DEPLOYMENT's own env vars
# (`npx convex env set` — MP_*, EMAIL_*, MAGIC_LINK_HMAC_KEY,
# ZEPHYRA_ACADEMIA_URL). Those live server-side, are shared mutable state, and
# are never read from any file.

# Written by `npx convex dev` on first run. Shared dev backend for the team.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:xxx

# The URLs the apps consume. `pnpm convex:sync` copies these outward, so keep them
# correct HERE and let the script do the rest.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://xxx.convex.cloud
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://xxx.convex.site
